    kind: work_item  # af5a
    title: "WI-sukav A2 alternative: per-edge virtual_dispatch flag in extends edges"  # af5a
    status: needs_human_review  # af5a
    priority: 4  # af5a
    parent:  # af5a
    tags:  # af5a
    - analysis_quality  # af5a
    - cross_language_linkers  # af5a
    before: []  # af5a
    duplicate_of: []  # af5a
    not_duplicate_of: []  # af5a
    pr_ref:  # af5a
    description: "Alternative framing of the WI-sukav fix. A1 (per-language flag table in type_hierarchy linker) ships first; A2 is the cleaner long-term direction once C++ analyzer infrastructure justifies the per-method tracking.\n\nDELIVERABLES:\n(1) Each analyzer emits 'extends' edges with meta.virtual_dispatch: True/False. Java/Python/Kotlin/Ruby always set True. Go always sets False. C++ computes from 'virtual' keyword presence per method. C# tracks 'virtual'/'override' modifier.\n\n(2) type_hierarchy.py reads edge.meta.virtual_dispatch and gates dispatches_to creation accordingly. Removes the per-language flag table introduced in A1.\n\n(3) Allows per-method overrides (e.g., a C++ class with both virtual and non-virtual methods).\n\nCURRENT STATUS: needs_human_review because the value of A2 over A1 depends on whether C++/C# per-method tracking actually pays off. Defer until A1 ships and bakeoff signals tell us whether per-method granularity is worth the migration cost."  # af5a
    fields: {}  # af5a
- op: discuss  # 92cf
  at: '2026-04-07T23:31:58Z'  # 92cf
